  "description": "The energy trade-off that any pair-term lower bound must price. The penalty for a mean-beta-gap deviation is quadratic and of order n^{3/2} against a prize of order sqrt n, so a maximiser's mean gap is pinned to 2 + O(1/sqrt n). Also runs the discriminator between that model's shrinking-excess prediction and #7279's growing measurement.",
